# Tests

- Write the failing test first, show it failing, then make it pass. Paste both runs in the PR.
- Test behavior, not implementation. Exercise real entry points (e.g. call the MCP tool, not just import it).
- Every guard/gate gets a deny-path test: error, timeout, malformed input, empty input.
- Never add `skip`, `xfail`, or loosen assertions to get green. Never lower `--cov-fail-under` or mutation thresholds.
- Tests must run offline with no API keys; live-model tests are marked and deselected by default.
- No network, no wall-clock sleeps, no order dependence. Use fixtures with fixed seeds.
